      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this needs to be split before review.\n\nThe direct branch commit endpoint may fill a real missing use case: applying a batch of file operations directly to a branch without cloning, guarded by push permission, optimistic base checking, ref validation, and commit validation.\n\nThe review endpoint is different. Gerrit already has a mature server-side review workflow for file edits through change edits: ChangeEdits / ChangeEditModifier / ChangeEditUtil / PublishChangeEdit. It is multi-step, but it is existing API surface and has been used for years. I do not think we should add a parallel one shot review workflow in the same change.\n\nThis is also around 1200 LoC, which makes it hard to review API shape, permission semantics, commit validation, direct ref updates, base-revision behavior, and review workflow semantics all at once.\n\nPlease split this:\n\n1. First change: direct branch commit only.\n2. Drop/defer content:review.\n3. Reuse as much of the existing inline-edit/tree code path as possible even for the direct branch commit path.\n4. If content:review is still desired later, send it as a separate change and route it through CreateChange.CommitTreeSupplier instead of manually creating a change with ChangeInserter.",
      "revId": "f7639b53e2909b1a89c43adc4314d6560c65fc30",
